public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# A closed point cut out set-theoretically isolated by an ideal sheaf

Let `X` be a Noetherian scheme, let `x ∈ X` be a closed point and let `I` be a quasi-coherent
sheaf of ideals whose stalk at `x` is the whole maximal ideal `𝔪_x`. Then the closed subscheme
`A = V(I)` splits, scheme theoretically, as

`A = x ⊔ Z`

with `x` the *reduced* point — `Spec κ(x)` — and `Z ⊂ A` the complementary open and closed
subscheme, supported on `Supp(I) ∖ {x}`.

This is **Step 5 of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FH5]**, in the generality in which that step is
used. There `X` is smooth projective of dimension `d` over a field, `x` is a closed point,
`s_1, …, s_d` are global sections of a very ample `ℒ` whose germs generate `𝔪_x ℒ_x`, and
`A = H_1 ∩ … ∩ H_d` is the scheme-theoretic intersection of their zero schemes; the hypothesis
used is exactly that the stalk of the ideal sheaf of `A` at `x` is `𝔪_x`, which is what
"`s_1, …, s_d` generate `𝔪_x ℒ_x`" says once the local equations of the `H_i` are read off a
trivialization of `ℒ` at `x`. The source states the conclusion in one sentence and leaves the
argument implicit.

## Main results

* `TopologicalSpace.isOpen_singleton_of_isClosed_of_forall_specializes_eq`: in a Noetherian,
  quasi-sober space a closed point admitting no proper generalization is isolated. This is where
  the finiteness of the set of irreducible components does the work; a pointwise dimension bound
  would not suffice.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isField_stalk_subscheme_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal`: the
  local ring of `V(I)` at `x` is the residue field `κ(x)`, hence a field.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isClopen_singleton_subscheme`: `{x}` is open and
  closed in `V(I)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_isOpenImmersion_pieces_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal`:
  **the splitting `A = x ⊔ Z`**, presented as the two open immersions with disjoint ranges
  covering `A` that the additivity of the fundamental cycle consumes, the first of them from the
  reduced point `Stacks.Chow.integralComponentAt x` and over the closed immersion
  `Spec κ(x) ⟶ X`.
* `Stacks.Chow.exists_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_eq_add_integralComponentAt` and
  `Stacks.Chow.exists_mk_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_eq_add_integralComponentAt`:
  `[A]_k = [x]_k + [Z]_k` in `Z_k(X)` and in `A_k(X)`, which is the form Steps 7 and 8 of
  Stacks 0FH5 use.

## Implementation notes

**The hypothesis is on the stalk of the ideal sheaf, not on sections.** The stalk is
`AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk`, the ideal of `𝒪_{X,x}` generated by the germs of the
sections of `I`, and the hypothesis `I.stalk x = 𝔪_x` is the local form of the source's
"`s_1, …, s_d` generate `𝔪_x ℒ_x`". Nothing below mentions an invertible module or a linear
system: the splitting depends only on the ideal sheaf.

**Why the point is reduced, and how it is recognised.** `𝒪_{A,x}` is the quotient of `𝒪_{X,x}`
by the stalk of the ideal sheaf — this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.ker_stalkMap_subschemeι_eq_stalk` together with the
surjectivity on stalks of a closed immersion — so under the hypothesis it is `𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_x`,
a field. The open subscheme of `A` on the isolated point `{x}` therefore has a single stalk and
that stalk is a field, so it is reduced; a closed immersion with reduced source cuts out the
reduced induced structure on its image
(`AlgebraicGeometry.ker_eq_vanishingIdeal_of_reduced_closed_immersion`, the uniqueness half of
Stacks 01J3), and the image is `{x}`, so the kernel is `Stacks.Chow.integralComponentAt x`. That
is how the first piece is identified with the reduced point rather than merely with *some*
closed subscheme supported at `x`, which is what makes the cycle `[x]` appear with multiplicity
one.

**Where the Noetherian hypothesis enters.** Only in the isolation of `x` inside `A`: a point
whose local ring is a field is a generic point of `A`, and `{x}`, being closed, is then an
irreducible component of `A`; it is *open* because a Noetherian space has finitely many
irreducible components, so the union of the others is closed. On a non-Noetherian scheme the
conclusion fails, and the source's `X` is projective over a field, hence Noetherian.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FH5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FH5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01J3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01J3)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace TopologicalSpace

/-- **In a Noetherian quasi-sober space a closed point with no proper generalization is
isolated.** The closure of such a point is an irreducible component, because every irreducible
closed set containing it is the closure of a point specializing to it; and an irreducible
component of a Noetherian space contains a nonempty open of the space, because the union of the
remaining components is closed, there being finitely many of them.

The finiteness is essential: in `𝔸²` over a field every closed point is closed and has no
proper generalization inside its own closure, and none of them is isolated — what fails there is
that `{x}` is not a component of `𝔸²`. -/
@[sga "1 IV 6.3" "special case"]
theorem isOpen_singleton_of_isClosed_of_forall_specializes_eq {α : Type*} [TopologicalSpace α]
    [NoetherianSpace α] [QuasiSober α] {x : α} (hcl : IsClosed ({x} : Set α))
    (hgen : ∀ y : α, y ⤳ x → y = x) : IsOpen ({x} : Set α) := by
  have hmem : ({x} : Set α) ∈ irreducibleComponents α := by
    refine ⟨isIrreducible_singleton, fun Z hZ hxZ ↦ ?_⟩
    have hcZ : IsIrreducible (closure Z) := hZ.closure
    have hη : closure ({hcZ.genericPoint} : Set α) = closure Z :=
      hcZ.isGenericPoint_genericPoint isClosed_closure
    have hsp : hcZ.genericPoint ⤳ x :=
      specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr (by rw [hη]; exact subset_closure (hxZ rfl))
    have h1 : closure Z = ({x} : Set α) := by rw [← hη, hgen _ hsp, hcl.closure_eq]
    exact subset_closure.trans h1.le
  obtain ⟨o, hoopen, ⟨y, hy⟩, hosub⟩ :=
    NoetherianSpace.exists_isOpen_nonempty_subset_irreducibleComponent ({x} : Set α) hmem
  obtain rfl : y = x := hosub hy
  exact hosub.antisymm (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hy) ▸ hoopen

end TopologicalSpace

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)

/-- **The local ring of `V(I)` at a point where the stalk of `I` is the whole maximal ideal is
the residue field there.** The stalk map of the closed immersion `V(I) ⟶ X` is surjective with
kernel the stalk of `I`, so the target is `𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_x`. -/
theorem isField_stalk_subscheme_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal (a : I.subscheme)
    (h : IdealSheafData.stalk I (I.subschemeι a) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι a))) :
    IsField ↑(I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk a) := by
  have hker : RingHom.ker (I.subschemeι.stalkMap a).hom =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ↑(X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι a)) := by
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.ker_stalkMap_subschemeι_eq_stalk I a, h]
  have h1 := Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective (I.subschemeι.stalkMap a).hom
    (I.subschemeι.stalkMap_surjective a)
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ↑(I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk a))
  rw [IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_comap] at h1
  rw [IsLocalRing.isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq, ← h1, ← hker, eq_bot_iff,
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
  intro z hz
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_bot]
  exact RingHom.mem_ker.mp hz

/-- **A point where the stalk of `I` is the whole maximal ideal has no proper generalization in
`V(I)`.** Its local ring there is a field, so the spectrum of that local ring is a single point,
and the points of `V(I)` specializing to it are exactly the image of that spectrum. -/
theorem eq_of_specializes_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal (a : I.subscheme)
    (h : IdealSheafData.stalk I (I.subschemeι a) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι a)))
    (b : I.subscheme) (hb : b ⤳ a) : b = a := by
  let : Field ↑(I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk a) :=
    (I.isField_stalk_subscheme_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal a h).toField
  have : Subsingleton ↥(Spec (I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk a)) :=
    inferInstanceAs (Subsingleton (PrimeSpectrum ↑(I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk a)))
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ : b ∈ Set.range (I.subscheme.fromSpecStalk a) := by
    rwa [Scheme.range_fromSpecStalk]
  calc b = I.subscheme.fromSpecStalk a q := hq.symm
    _ = I.subscheme.fromSpecStalk a
          (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk a)) :=
        congrArg _ (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
    _ = a := Scheme.fromSpecStalk_closedPoint

/-- **A closed point where the stalk of `I` is the whole maximal ideal is isolated in `V(I)`.**
It is closed there because `V(I) ⟶ X` is an embedding, it has no proper generalization there by
`eq_of_specializes_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal`, and the topology of `V(I)` is Noetherian. -/
theorem isClopen_singleton_subscheme [IsNoetherian X] (a : I.subscheme)
    (hcl : IsClosed ({I.subschemeι a} : Set X))
    (h : IdealSheafData.stalk I (I.subschemeι a) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι a))) :
    IsClopen ({a} : Set I.subscheme) := by
  have : NoetherianSpace I.subscheme :=
    Topology.IsInducing.noetherianSpace I.subschemeι.isClosedEmbedding.isInducing
  have hclA : IsClosed ({a} : Set I.subscheme) :=
    I.subschemeι.isClosedEmbedding.isClosed_iff_image_isClosed.mpr (by rwa [Set.image_singleton])
  exact ⟨hclA, TopologicalSpace.isOpen_singleton_of_isClosed_of_forall_specializes_eq hclA
    (I.eq_of_specializes_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal a h)⟩

/-- **A closed point where the stalk of `I` is the whole maximal ideal lies in the support of
`I`.** The stalk of an ideal sheaf is the unit ideal exactly off the support, and the maximal
ideal is not the unit ideal. -/
theorem mem_support_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal (x : X)
    (h : IdealSheafData.stalk I x = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ↑(X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    x ∈ I.support := by
  by_contra hns
  rw [← AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_not_mem_support, h] at hns
  exact (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal ↑(X.presheaf.stalk x)).ne_top hns

/-- **The open subscheme of `V(I)` on an isolated point with field local ring is reduced.** Every
point of that open subscheme is the given one, and its stalk there is the stalk of `V(I)`, a
field. -/
theorem isReduced_opens_singleton_subscheme (a : I.subscheme)
    (h : IdealSheafData.stalk I (I.subschemeι a) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ↑(X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι a)))
    (U : I.subscheme.Opens) (hU : ∀ z : I.subscheme, z ∈ U → z = a) :
    IsReduced U.toScheme := by
  have hfield := I.isField_stalk_subscheme_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal a h
  have : ∀ z : U.toScheme, _root_.IsReduced ↑(U.toScheme.presheaf.stalk z) := by
    intro z
    have hz : z.1 = a := hU z.1 z.2
    let : Field ↑(I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk z.1) :=
      (show IsField ↑(I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk z.1) by rwa [hz]).toField
    exact isReduced_of_injective ((U.stalkIso z).hom.hom)
      (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (U.stalkIso z).hom).1
  exact isReduced_of_isReduced_stalk U.toScheme

/-- **The splitting `V(I) = x ⊔ Z` of Step 5 of [Stacks, Tag 0FH5].** If the stalk of the
quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals `I` at the closed point `x` of the Noetherian scheme `X` is the
whole maximal ideal `𝔪_x`, then the closed subscheme `V(I)` is the disjoint union of two open
and closed pieces: the first is the *reduced* point `x`, in the sense that its closed immersion
into `X` cuts out `Stacks.Chow.integralComponentAt x`, and the second is supported on
`Supp(I) ∖ {x}`.

The pieces are presented as open immersions into `V(I)` whose composites with `V(I) ⟶ X` are
closed immersions, which is the shape
`Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_eq_add_of_isOpenImmersion_pieces` consumes. -/
theorem exists_isOpenImmersion_pieces_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal [IsNoetherian X] (x : X)
    (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set X))
    (h : IdealSheafData.stalk I x = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ↑(X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    ∃ (A₁ A₂ : Scheme.{u}) (g₁ : A₁ ⟶ I.subscheme) (g₂ : A₂ ⟶ I.subscheme),
      ∃ (_ : IsOpenImmersion g₁) (_ : IsOpenImmersion g₂)
        (_ : IsClosedImmersion (g₁ ≫ I.subschemeι))
        (_ : IsClosedImmersion (g₂ ≫ I.subschemeι)),
        (g₁ ≫ I.subschemeι).ker = Stacks.Chow.integralComponentAt x ∧
          Set.range (g₂ ≫ I.subschemeι).base = (I.support : Set X) \ {x} ∧
          Disjoint (Set.range g₁.base) (Set.range g₂.base) ∧
          Set.range g₁.base ∪ Set.range g₂.base = Set.univ := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ : x ∈ Set.range I.subschemeι := by
    rw [IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
    exact I.mem_support_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal x h
  have h' : IdealSheafData.stalk I (I.subschemeι a) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ↑(X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι a)) := by rwa [ha]
  have hclopen := I.isClopen_singleton_subscheme a (by rwa [ha]) h'
  let U₁ : I.subscheme.Opens := ⟨{a}, hclopen.2⟩
  let U₂ : I.subscheme.Opens := ⟨{a}ᶜ, hclopen.1.isOpen_compl⟩
  have hci : ∀ U : I.subscheme.Opens, IsClosed (U : Set I.subscheme) → IsClosedImmersion U.ι :=
    fun U hU ↦ IsClosedImmersion.of_isPreimmersion _ (by rwa [Scheme.Opens.range_ι])
  have himg : ∀ U : I.subscheme.Opens,
      Set.range (U.ι ≫ I.subschemeι).base = I.subschemeι.base '' (U : Set I.subscheme) := by
    intro U
    simp [Set.range_comp, Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
  have : IsReduced U₁.toScheme :=
    I.isReduced_opens_singleton_subscheme a h' U₁ fun z hz ↦ hz
  have hrange₁ : Set.range (U₁.ι ≫ I.subschemeι).base = ({x} : Set X) := by
    rw [himg]
    change I.subschemeι.base '' ({a} : Set I.subscheme) = _
    rw [Set.image_singleton, ha]
  have := hci U₁ hclopen.1
  have := hci U₂ hclopen.2.isClosed_compl
  refine ⟨U₁.toScheme, U₂.toScheme, U₁.ι, U₂.ι, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    inferInstance, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [ker_eq_vanishingIdeal_of_reduced_closed_immersion, Stacks.Chow.integralComponentAt]
    congr 1
    refine TopologicalSpace.Closeds.ext ?_
    rw [Scheme.Hom.support_ker, hrange₁]
    simp
  · rw [himg]
    change I.subschemeι.base '' ({a}ᶜ : Set I.subscheme) = _
    rw [← Set.range_sdiff_image I.subschemeι.isClosedEmbedding.injective, Set.image_singleton, ha,
      IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
  · rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι, Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    exact disjoint_compl_right
  · rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι, Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    exact Set.union_compl_self _

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-- **`[V(I)]_k = [x]_k + [Z]_k`**, the cycle-level form of the splitting of Step 5 of
[Stacks, Tag 0FH5]. The coefficient of `[x]` is one: the piece of `V(I)` at `x` is the reduced
point, so the cycle of its closed immersion into `X` is the cycle of
`Stacks.Chow.integralComponentAt x`.

The two inputs are the splitting
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_isOpenImmersion_pieces_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal`
and the additivity of the fundamental cycle over such a splitting,
`Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_eq_add_of_isOpenImmersion_pieces`. -/
theorem exists_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_eq_add_integralComponentAt
    (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p]
    [IsNoetherian X] (I : X.IdealSheafData) (x : X) (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set X))
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk I x =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ↑(X.presheaf.stalk x)) (k : ℤ) :
    ∃ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (ι₂ : Z ⟶ X) (_ : IsClosedImmersion ι₂),
      Set.range ι₂.base = (I.support : Set X) \ {x} ∧
        cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p I.subschemeι k =
          cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p (integralComponentAt x).subschemeι k +
            cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p ι₂ k := by
  obtain ⟨A₁, A₂, g₁, g₂, _, _, _, hc₂, hker, hrange₂, hdisj, hcover⟩ :=
    I.exists_isOpenImmersion_pieces_of_stalk_eq_maximalIdeal x hx h
  refine ⟨A₂, g₂ ≫ I.subschemeι, hc₂, hrange₂, ?_⟩
  rw [cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_eq_add_of_isOpenImmersion_pieces C p I.subschemeι
    (g₁ ≫ I.subschemeι) (g₂ ≫ I.subschemeι) g₁ g₂ rfl rfl hdisj hcover k]
  congr 1
  rw [cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_ker C p (g₁ ≫ I.subschemeι) k, hker]

/-- **`[V(I)]_k = [x]_k + [Z]_k` in the Chow group `A_k(X)`**, which is the form Steps 7 and 8 of
[Stacks, Tag 0FH5] use: the class of the complete intersection splits as the class of the chosen
closed point plus the class of the residual closed subscheme. -/
theorem exists_mk_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_eq_add_integralComponentAt
    (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p]
    [IsNoetherian X] (I : X.IdealSheafData) (x : X) (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set X))
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk I x =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ↑(X.presheaf.stalk x)) (k : ℤ) :
    ∃ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (ι₂ : Z ⟶ X) (_ : IsClosedImmersion ι₂),
      Set.range ι₂.base = (I.support : Set X) \ {x} ∧
        QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rationalEquivalences C p k)
            (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p I.subschemeι k) =
          QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rationalEquivalences C p k)
              (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p (integralComponentAt x).subschemeι k) +
            QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rationalEquivalences C p k)
              (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p ι₂ k) := by
  obtain ⟨Z, ι₂, hc₂, hrange₂, heq⟩ :=
    exists_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_eq_add_integralComponentAt C p I x hx h k
  exact ⟨Z, ι₂, hc₂, hrange₂, by rw [heq, map_add]⟩

end Stacks.Chow

end
